<title>CHINA: Shanghai Huili 96 net down 67.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Shanghai Huili 96 net down 67.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of yuan unless stated, against 1995 figures)</p>
<p> Turnover	    259.281	 vs	  499.593</p>
<p> Net profit	   15.727	 vs	  48.695</p>
<p> Net assets per share    1.50  yuan</p>
<p> Earnings per share	0.095 yuan</p>
<p>(The company listed its B shares on June 28, 1996)</p>
<p>Company name: Shanghai Huili Building Materials Co Ltd</p>
<p>Note: The results were published in a company statement on Thursday and the figures are based on domestic accounting standards. It did not give figures based on international accounting standards, or comparative figures for net assets per share and earnings per share.</p>
<p>The company's board of directors have proposed no cash dividend or bonus shares, pending approval at a shareholders meeting.</p>
</text>
